<title>USA: H.J. Heinz Q4 net share loss after charges.</title>
<headline>H.J. Heinz Q4 net share loss after charges.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.61   profit	 $0.45</p>
<p> Net loss		 229,566   profit     170,199</p>
<p> Sales		  2,446,651		2,536,557</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 373,703		  377,156</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.81   profit	 $1.75</p>
<p> Net profit	     301,871   profit     659,319</p>
<p> Sales		  9,357,007		9,112,265</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 373,703		  377,156</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1997 ended April 30, Q4 1996 ended May 1.</p>
<p>Fiscal 1997 restructuring and related costs, net of gains recognized on the sale of certain non-strategic assets,  resulted in a full- year and fourth quarter effect of $0.95 per share and $0.94 per share, respectively.</p>
<p>The company said that excluding the costs, net income and earnings per share in Q4 would have been $186.2 million and $0.50 per share.</p>
<p>First Call estimates EPS estimates for Q4 were $0.48 ---New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
